== 1. effective integer thresholds ==
  in-scope  delta>=0.0: passes iff net (wins-losses) >= 0
  out-scope delta>=-0.05: passes iff net (wins-losses) >= 0
  harmful pair (n=10, delta<-0.05): harmful iff net <= -1  (one net loss)
  replay (n=5): successes_with>=3 and net>=2 (integer rule in inheritance/replay.py:44-46)

== 2. float boundary: PR #28 inheritance/regression.py:231 `drop = 1.0 - successes / len(tasks)` ==
  tau_r=0.02: failures allowed (code float) <= 0 ; exact rational <= 0  drop(38/40)=0.050000000000000044
  tau_r=0.03: failures allowed (code float) <= 1 ; exact rational <= 1  drop(38/40)=0.050000000000000044
  tau_r=0.05: failures allowed (code float) <= 1 ; exact rational <= 2  drop(38/40)=0.050000000000000044

== 3. stage-2 pass region (repo bootstrap, seed 0, 10k) ==
  minimum passing point estimate: 0.20
  losses=0: passes iff wins >= 4
  losses=1: passes iff wins >= 7
  losses=2: passes iff wins >= 9
  losses=3: passes iff wins >= 11

== 4. model-based gate pass probabilities ==
Model (assumption-laden, NOT data): each task independently falls in one of four
paired cells: both succeed, both fail, win (with=1,without=0), loss (with=0,without=1).
G0 success p; discordance d = P(win)+P(loss); net effect e = P(win)-P(loss).
win=(d+e)/2, loss=(d-e)/2. Out-of-scope tasks: e=0, same d. T_reg tasks are G0
successes, so per-task with-trait failure prob f = loss/p. Stages treated as
independent (disjoint task sets). Interaction stage ignored (single eligible).

